Two rendering bugs fixed in the KB/examples (both verified against v10.3.0):
- **Table cells**: an unstyled `<Td>` is NOT transparent — POM emits no fill and PowerPoint's default table style takes over (white fill, black text, row banding) = a white island on a themed deck. EVERY `<Td>` must set `backgroundColor` + `color`. Examples/table.yaml/notes now enforce header=`$surfaceAlt`/`$textMain`, body=`$surface`/`$textMuted`|`$textMain`, `cellBorder.color="$border"`.
- **Chart axis text is ALWAYS black**: `renderPptx/nodes/chart.js` hardcodes category+value axis `textStyle.color` to `000000` and gridlines `888888` — no XML override. Invisible on dark slides. Fix: on a dark palette wrap `<Chart>` in `<VStack backgroundColor="$chartSurface" padding="16" borderRadius="12">` (shrink chart w/h by ~2*padding). Light palettes need no wrapper. `sparkline="true"` hides axes entirely (alternative). Default deck is now LIGHT (corporate-slate) which sidesteps this.

